; The yard and the closed mine beyond the north window, as real geometry.
;
; Before this, the middle and far distance were two painted pixel shields (the
; mineworks at 9 m, the slope at 26 m); every texel of them read as a block the
; size of a hand. The plan (3.2) asks for depth from simple geometry and fog:
;
;   middle  rails to the shaft, one switch lamp           8 .. 48 m out
;   far     the headframe, engine house, stack, spoil      45 .. 75 m out
;   very far two ridge lines                               150 .. 230 m out
;
; Everything is unshaded: nothing out here is lit from inside (the mine has
; been shut since 1885) and the room's lights never reach it. The scene fog
; does the rest: the nearer a thing is, the darker it stands against the sky.
; Nothing here has collision, and the column the figure stands in (x = -1.5,
; just outside the glass) is untouched; everything here is far behind it.

